#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to use stretch to defer timing resolution with dynamic circuits"
msgstr "Paano gamitin ang stretch para i-defer ang resolusyon ng timing sa mga dynamic na circuit"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deferred timing resolution using stretch"
msgstr "Naantalang resolusyon ng timing gamit ang stretch"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deferred timing resolution using stretch {#deferred-timing-resolution-using-stretch}"
msgstr "Naantalang resolusyon ng timing gamit ang stretch {#deferred-timing-resolution-using-stretch}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The OpenQASM 3 language specification contains a `stretch` type with which you can specify relative timing of operations instead of absolute timing. Support for `stretch` as durations for [`Delay`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.Delay) instructions was added in [Qiskit v2.0.0](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/release-notes/2.0#200). The concrete value of a stretch duration is resolved at compile time, after the exact duration of calibrated gates are known.  The compiler tries to minimize the stretch duration, subject to timing constraints on one or more qubits. You can then express gate designs such as evenly spacing gates (for example, to implement a higher-order echo decoupling sequence), left-aligning a sequence of gates, or applying a gate for the duration of some sub-circuit, without knowing the exact timing.\n"
msgstr "Ang OpenQASM 3 language specification ay naglalaman ng uri na `stretch` kung saan maaari kang tumukoy ng relatibong timing ng mga operasyon sa halip na absolute timing. Ang suporta para sa `stretch` bilang mga tagal para sa mga instruksyon na [`Delay`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.Delay) ay idinagdag sa [Qiskit v2.0.0](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/release-notes/2.0#200). Ang konkretong halaga ng tagal ng stretch ay nareresolta sa compile time, pagkatapos malaman ang eksaktong tagal ng mga calibrated na gate. Sinisikap ng compiler na i-minimize ang tagal ng stretch, batay sa mga hadlang sa timing ng isa o higit pang mga qubit. Maaari ka na ring mag-ekspresa ng mga disenyo ng gate tulad ng pantay na paglalagay ng mga gate (halimbawa, para ipatupad ang mas mataas na antas ng echo decoupling sequence), pag-align sa kaliwa ng isang pagkakasunod-sunod ng mga gate, o pag-apply ng gate para sa tagal ng ilang sub-circuit, nang hindi alam ang eksaktong timing.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Examples {#examples}"
msgstr "Mga Halimbawa {#examples}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamical decoupling {#dynamical-decoupling}"
msgstr "Dynamical decoupling {#dynamical-decoupling}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A common use case of `stretch` is to apply dynamical decoupling to an idling qubit while another qubit is undergoing conditional operations.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang karaniwang gamit ng `stretch` ay ang pag-apply ng dynamical decoupling sa isang qubit na walang ginagawa habang ang isa pang qubit ay sumasailalim sa mga kondisyonal na operasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, we can use `stretch` to apply an XX dynamical decoupling sequence to qubit 1, for the duration of the conditional block applied to qubit 0, as illustrated by the following diagram:\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa, maaari nating gamitin ang `stretch` para mag-apply ng XX dynamical decoupling sequence sa qubit 1, para sa tagal ng kondisyonal na bloke na inilapat sa qubit 0, gaya ng inilalarawan ng sumusunod na diagram:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Image illustrating the following circuit](/docs/images/guides/stretch/stretch.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Larawang nagpapakita ng sumusunod na circuit](/docs/images/guides/stretch/stretch.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The corresponding circuit would look like the following. Note that a pair of barriers is needed to define the boundaries of this relative timing.\n"
msgstr "Ang kaukulang circuit ay magiging ganito. Tandaan na kailangan ng pares ng mga barrier para tukuyin ang mga hangganan ng relatibong timing na ito.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scheduling alignment {#scheduling-alignment}"
msgstr "Pag-align ng scheduling {#scheduling-alignment}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example uses `stretch` to ensure a sequence of gates between two barriers are left-aligned, whatever their actual durations are:\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng halimbawang ito ang `stretch` para matiyak na ang isang pagkakasunod-sunod ng mga gate sa pagitan ng dalawang barrier ay naka-align sa kaliwa, anuman ang kanilang aktwal na mga tagal:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid " When using `stretch` with Qiskit Runtime, any remainder resulting from a stretch resolution is added to the first delay that uses the stretch.\n"
msgid " When using `stretch` with IBM Quantum Compute Service, any remainder resulting from a stretch resolution is added to the first delay that uses the stretch.\n"
msgstr " Kapag gumagamit ng `stretch` kasama ang Qiskit Runtime, ang anumang natitira mula sa resolusyon ng stretch ay idinadagdag sa unang delay na gumagamit ng stretch.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example:\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"    circuit.barrier(q0, q1)\n"
"    circuit.delay(100, q0)\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 26\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 25\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 25\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.barrier(q0, q1)\n"
"     ```\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```python\n"
"    a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"    circuit.barrier(q0, q1)\n"
"    circuit.delay(100, q0)\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 26\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 25\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 25\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.barrier(q0, q1)\n"
"     ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The above code resolves to a value of 25 with a remainder of 1. The first delay`[a]` will have the remainder added.\n"
msgstr "Ang code sa itaas ay nareresolta sa halagang 25 na may natitira na 1. Ang unang delay`[a]` ay magkakaroon ng naidagdag na natitira.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stretch resolution equation:  $a + 8 + a + 8 + a + 8 = 100   =   3*a + 24$\n"
msgstr "Equation ng resolusyon ng stretch:  $a + 8 + a + 8 + a + 8 = 100   =   3*a + 24$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr "</DoqAdmonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "View stretch values in Qiskit Runtime {#view-stretch-values-in-qiskit-runtime}"
msgid "View stretch values in IBM Quantum Compute Service {#view-stretch-values-in-ibm-quantum-compute-service}"
msgstr "Tingnan ang mga stretch value sa Qiskit Runtime {#view-stretch-values-in-qiskit-runtime}"

